cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these model weights, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ednhemo: small-hemorrhage-aware intracranial hemorrhage detection on CT"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aimenachraff-jpg/ednhemo"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/ednhemo/"
authors:
  - family-names: Chekalil
    given-names: Aimene Charef Eddine
  - family-names: Ouadah
    given-names: Mustapha
keywords:
  - intracranial hemorrhage
  - CT
  - segmentation
  - U-Net
  - deep learning
  - BHSD
abstract: >-
  A 2D U-Net that segments intracranial hemorrhages on non-contrast head CT and
  reports them lesion by lesion (volume, size class, confidence). The default
  checkpoint was trained with four small-hemorrhage slices guaranteed in every
  batch of eight, which recovers 19 more lesions than the reference model on
  the official 96-scan BHSD test set.
